preConditionHook:
// RISK WHAT THE MOVE BEING FADED ALREADY MADE. Brooks: "risk about five points
// to make five points, expecting a test of the breakout" -- the protective stop
// is sized to the run, not to a fixed dollar amount and not to one bar.
//
// The book measures the breakout's start-to-extreme leg, which needs a leg
// measurement; the mechanizable stand-in is the high-low SPAN of the last
// runLookback bars, over the window ENDING ONE BAR AGO so the bar being judged
// cannot widen its own stop. runFraction 1.0 is "risk as much as the run".
//
// Not StopAtSignalBarRangeMultiple (ONE bar's range), not SessionAvgBarRangeStop
// (the MEAN bar range so far today), not AvgDailyRangeFractionStop (an N-SESSION
// average daily range), not AtrProfitTarget / AtrTrailingStop (a rolling N-bar
// ATR, and a target and a trail). This is an N-BAR SPAN and a fixed stop.
//
// Direction-agnostic, so both sides are identical text, as StopLoss is.
// BigPointValue is the raw multiplier and is NOT currency-converted while
// OpenPositionProfit is -- preserved as in AtrProfitTarget.
//
// The Extremes loop is seeded on the window's FIRST bar (index 1) and scans the
// rest with the tolerance-carrying strict comparison, matching EL's Extremes
// source, as StopBeyondRecentRangeExtreme and RoomToRangeTargetFilter do.
runHi = high[1];
runLo = low[1];
for (int i = 2; i <= (int)runLookback; ++i) {
    if (el_gt(high[i], runHi)) runHi = high[i];
    if (el_lt(low[i], runLo)) runLo = low[i];
}
runSize = runHi - runLo;
